@adam4813 For example, the third result on Google for me is https://gist.github.com/underscorediscovery/46e4f5b4e3e6de7ad50d which is just a cpp file that assumes the opengl functions are available.

@mattiascibien Yes, the Windows SDK will automatically add it to the link path so a simple `opengl32.lib` link reference will work fine. `find_library()` will also work from CMake just fine, with and without the `opengl` package installed.

The only functional difference is to make `opengl32.lib` implicitly linked when using MSBuild (see #306).
